## File Management & Operations

### Theory: Data Set Lifecycle

**Typical Lifecycle:**

```
CREATE → PROCESS → BACKUP → ARCHIVE → DELETE

1. CREATE
   └─ Allocate space
   └─ Set attributes
   └─ Catalog if permanent

2. PROCESS
   └─ Read/write data
   └─ Modify as needed
   └─ Generate output

3. BACKUP
   └─ Copy to tape
   └─ For disaster recovery
   └─ Legal requirement

4. ARCHIVE
   └─ Move to slower storage
   └─ Long-term retention
   └─ Compliance

5. DELETE
   └─ When retention expired
   └─ Reclaim space
   └─ Cost reduction
```

**Practical File Operations:**

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* FILE MANAGEMENT WORKFLOW
//*==================================================

//FILEMGMT JOB (8000,STORAGE),'FILE MANAGEMENT',
//              CLASS=C,
//              TIME=(0,120)

//*==================================================
//* STEP 1: CREATE BACKUP OF CURRENT DATA
//*==================================================

//BACKUP   EXEC PGM=BACKUP-UTILITY

//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*

//* Source data (Production)
//SOURCE   DD DSN=COMPANY.PRODUCTION.DATA,
//             DISP=SHR,
//             UNIT=3390

//* Backup on tape
//BACKUPVOL DD DSN=BACKUP.&SYSDATE..DATA,
//              DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//              UNIT=TAPE,
//              VOL=SER=BKTAPE1,
//              SPACE=(TRK,(50000,10000))

//REPORT   DD SYSOUT=*

//*==================================================
//* STEP 2: ARCHIVE OLD DATA (>90 days)
