### Q12: What do different HTTP status codes mean?

**Answer:**

**2xx - Success:**

```
200 OK
  └─ Request succeeded
  └─ Most common success response

201 Created
  └─ Resource created successfully
  └─ Used with POST requests
  └─ Should include Location header

202 Accepted
  └─ Request accepted but not yet processed
  └─ For async operations

204 No Content
  └─ Successful but no content to return
  └─ Common for DELETE requests
```

**3xx - Redirection:**

```
301 Moved Permanently
  └─ Resource permanently moved
  └─ Browser follows redirect automatically

302 Found
  └─ Temporary redirect
  └─ Browser follows redirect

304 Not Modified
  └─ Resource unchanged since last request
  └─ Use caching headers
  └─ No body sent
```

**4xx - Client Error:**

```
400 Bad Request
  └─ Invalid request format
  └─ Example: Malformed JSON

401 Unauthorized
  └─ Authentication required
  └─ Missing/invalid credentials
  └─ Redirect to login

403 Forbidden
  └─ Authenticated but lacking permission
  └─ User cannot access resource

404 Not Found
  └─ Resource doesn't exist
  └─ Check URL spelling

409 Conflict
  └─ Request conflicts with current state
  └─ Example: Duplicate username
```

**5xx - Server Error:**

```
500 Internal Server Error
  └─ Server error (unexpected)
  └─ Not client's fault
  └─ Typically transient

502 Bad Gateway
  └─ Server received invalid response
  └─ Often temporary

503 Service Unavailable
  └─ Server temporarily unavailable
  └─ Maintenance or overload

504 Gateway Timeout
  └─ Server didn't respond in time
  └─ Network/server issue
```

**Handling different status codes:**

```javascript
async function handleResponse(response) {
    switch (response.status) {
        case 200:
        case 201:
            // Success
            return await response.json();
            
        case 204:
            // No content
            return null;
            
        case 304:
            // Use cached version
            return getCachedData();
            
        case 400:
            const errors = await response.json();
            throw new ValidationError('Invalid input', errors);
            
        case 401:
            // Redirect to login
            window.location.href = '/login';
            throw new AuthError('Please login');
            
        case 403:
            throw new AuthError('Access denied');
            
        case 404:
            throw new NotFoundError('Resource not found');
            
        case 429:
            // Rate limited - retry after delay
            const retryAfter = response.headers.get('Retry-After');
            throw new RateLimitError(`Try again in ${retryAfter} seconds`);
            
        case 500:
        case 502:
        case 503:
            // Server error - retry
            throw new ServerError(`Server error ${response.status}`);
            
        default:
            throw new Error(`HTTP ${response.status}: ${response.statusText}`);
    }
}
```

