## CORS & Security

### Q14: What is CORS and how do you handle it?

**Answer:**

**CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing)** controls which domains can access your API.

**Why CORS exists:**

```
Security Issue:
  Malicious website could:
  ├─ Make requests to your bank.com
  ├─ Transfer money from your account
  ├─ Read your personal data

CORS Solution:
  └─ Server explicitly allows certain domains
  └─ Browser enforces these rules
```

**Simple vs Preflight requests:**

```
SIMPLE REQUEST (no preflight):
  ├─ GET, HEAD, POST only
  ├─ Simple headers
  ├─ No custom headers
  └─ Direct request to server

PREFLIGHT REQUEST (OPTIONS):
  ├─ PUT, PATCH, DELETE, etc.
  ├─ Custom headers
  ├─ Browser sends OPTIONS request first
  ├─ Server validates
  ├─ Then sends actual request
```

**Handling CORS on client:**

```javascript
// Request with credentials (cookies)
fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
    credentials: 'include', // Send cookies
    headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    }
})

// CORS headers browser will see:
// Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://mydomain.com
// Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
// Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET, POST, PUT
// Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, Authorization
```

**Server-side CORS setup (Express):**

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const cors = require('cors');

const app = express();

// Allow all domains (insecure)
app.use(cors());

// Allow specific domain (secure)
app.use(cors({
    origin: 'https://mydomain.com',
    credentials: true,
    methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'PATCH', 'DELETE'],
    allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization']
}));

// Manual CORS handling
app.use((req, res, next) => {
    res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', 'https://mydomain.com');
    res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true');
    res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Methods', 'GET, POST, PUT, DELETE');
    res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Headers', 'Content-Type, Authorization');
    
    // Handle preflight
    if (req.method === 'OPTIONS') {
        return res.sendStatus(200);
    }
    
    next();
});
```

**Common CORS errors:**

```
Error: "Access to XMLHttpRequest at 'https://api.com' from origin 
'https://mydomain.com' has been blocked by CORS policy"

Causes:
  1. Domain not in Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  2. Missing credentials header
  3. Headers not whitelisted
  4. Method not allowed
  5. Preflight failed
```

