### Q15: How do you prevent XSS and CSRF attacks in AJAX?

**Answer:**

**XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) - Injecting malicious scripts:**

```
Attack:
  User submits: <img src=x onerror="alert('hacked')">
  Server stores it as-is
  Other users see alert popup
  Attacker can steal cookies/data

Prevention:
  1. Escape HTML entities
  2. Validate input
  3. Use sanitization library
```

**XSS prevention in AJAX:**

```javascript
// VULNERABLE: Setting innerHTML with user data
const userComment = '<img src=x onerror="alert(\'hacked\')">';
document.getElementById('comments').innerHTML = userComment; // DANGEROUS

// SAFE: Using textContent
document.getElementById('comments').textContent = userComment; // Safe

// SAFE: Proper HTML escaping
function escapeHTML(text) {
    const map = {
        '&': '&amp;',
        '<': '&lt;',
        '>': '&gt;',
        '"': '&quot;',
        "'": '&#039;'
    };
    return text.replace(/[&<>"']/g, char => map[char]);
}

const safe = escapeHTML(userComment);
document.getElementById('comments').innerHTML = safe;

// Using libraries
import DOMPurify from 'dompurify';
const clean = DOMPurify.sanitize(userComment);
```

**CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery) - Forging requests:**

```
Attack:
  1. User logs into bank.com
  2. User opens malicious-site.com in another tab
  3. Malicious site makes hidden request: 
     POST /bank.com/transfer?amount=1000&to=attacker
  4. Browser sends cookies automatically
  5. Transfer goes through without user knowing

Prevention:
  1. Use CSRF tokens
  2. Check referrer header
  3. Use SameSite cookies
```

**CSRF token implementation:**

```html
<!-- HTML: Include CSRF token -->
<meta name="csrf-token" content="abc123xyz">
```

```javascript
// JavaScript: Send token with each request
async function safePost(url, data) {
    const token = document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content;
    
    const response = await fetch(url, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
            'Content-Type': 'application/json',
            'X-CSRF-Token': token // Send token in header
        },
        credentials: 'include', // Send cookies
        body: JSON.stringify(data)
    });
    
    return await response.json();
}
```

```javascript
// Server: Validate token
app.post('/api/transfer', (req, res) => {
    const token = req.headers['x-csrf-token'];
    
    // Verify token matches session
    if (!verifyCSRFToken(req.session.id, token)) {
        return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Invalid CSRF token' });
    }
    
    // Process transfer
    // ...
});
```

**SameSite cookies (modern approach):**

```javascript
// Server: Set SameSite attribute
res.cookie('sessionId', value, {
    httpOnly: true,      // Can't access from JS
    secure: true,        // HTTPS only
    sameSite: 'Strict'   // Can't send cross-site
    // 'Strict' = never send to other sites
    // 'Lax' = send with top-level navigation
    // 'None' = send cross-site (must use Secure)
});
```

