### Scenario 2: Real-Time Notifications System

**Business Requirement:**

```
System must:
├─ Check for new notifications frequently
├─ Update badge count in real-time
├─ Display notification without page reload
├─ Handle multiple simultaneous users
├─ Scale to thousands of users

User Flow:
├─ User logs in
├─ Browser starts polling server
├─ When new notification available
├─ Badge updates (e.g., "5 new")
├─ User sees notification in dropdown
└─ Clicking opens detailed view
```

**Theory: Polling vs WebSocket**

```
POLLING (AJAX):
├─ Client repeatedly asks: "Any new notifications?"
├─ Server responds: "Yes" or "No"
├─ Every 5-30 seconds typically
├─ Simple to implement
├─ Higher latency
├─ Higher server load

When to use Polling:
├─ Lower frequency updates (5+ seconds)
├─ Legacy server support
├─ Simpler infrastructure
├─ Mobile with battery concerns

WEBSOCKET (Advanced):
├─ Persistent connection
├─ Server pushes notifications
├─ Real-time (sub-second)
├─ Complex to implement
├─ Better for high-frequency updates
└─ More efficient
```

**AJAX Polling Implementation:**

