## Summary: AJAX Best Practices

**Do:**
- ✅ Use Fetch API over XMLHttpRequest
- ✅ Handle errors gracefully
- ✅ Show loading states
- ✅ Validate data server-side
- ✅ Use CSRF tokens
- ✅ Debounce frequent requests
- ✅ Cache when appropriate
- ✅ Implement retry logic

**Don't:**
- ❌ Trust client-side validation alone
- ❌ Send sensitive data in AJAX
- ❌ Make unbounded requests
- ❌ Ignore CORS/security headers
- ❌ Update UI without feedback
- ❌ Overuse AJAX (not every action needs it)
- ❌ Forget to handle network errors

**Real-World Impact:**
- User satisfaction ↑ (responsive UI)
- Bandwidth usage ↓ (partial updates)
- Server load ↑ (need efficiency)
- Development complexity ↑ (handle async)
- Scalability ↑ (with proper architecture)

Master these concepts and you'll build seamless, professional web applications!
